# masterlearn-ai

**A copy-paste protocol that turns any AI chatbot into a real tutor — for any subject.**

Most people use AI to learn by just... asking it questions. The AI explains things you already know, skips things you don't, and never actually checks if you learned anything. You *feel* like you're learning. You often aren't.

`masterlearn-ai` fixes that with one simple loop:

**Diagnose → Teach only the gap → Test immediately → Repeat.**

No app to install. No account. Just a block of text you paste into ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, or any AI, plus a companion system for studying on your own when you don't have AI access.

Works for HSC/A-Level Math, Physics, programming, a new language, an instrument, exam prep — anything with a body of knowledge and a way to test yourself on it.

---

## Why this works

- **A diagnostic first** finds your real gaps instead of assuming you're a total beginner or making you sit through material you already know.
- **Teaching only the gap** means no wasted time on things you've already mastered.
- **Testing after every single concept** — not at the end of a chapter — catches a misunderstanding while it's still cheap to fix.
- **Full working shown, every time** separates "actually understands it" from "got lucky" or "pattern-matched the answer."
- **Spaced revisits** (day 1, 3, 7, 21) push what you've learned into long-term memory instead of letting it evaporate after the session.

This is just applied learning science — diagnostic assessment, mastery learning, retrieval practice, spaced repetition — packaged as something you can actually use in 30 seconds.

---

## How to use it

### With an AI (see [`protocol-with-ai.md`](./protocol-with-ai.md))
Copy the prompt template, fill in your topic and your background in two brackets, paste it into any AI chat. That's the whole setup step. The AI then runs the full diagnose-teach-test loop with you.

### Studying alone (see [`protocol-solo-study.md`](./protocol-solo-study.md))
The same four-step loop, adapted for a textbook and no AI — for the hours when you don't have internet access or just want to self-test. Includes a self-grading rubric and a weekly log format.

### The rules (see [`rules.md`](./rules.md))
Four subject-agnostic principles behind the whole system: understand *why* not just *how*, never build on a shaky foundation, treat careless mistakes differently from real gaps, and always test — never just read.

---

## Quick start

1. Open `protocol-with-ai.md`
2. Copy the prompt block
3. Fill in `[TOPIC]` and `[your context]`
4. Paste into your AI of choice and start with the diagnostic

That's it — no setup, no tools, no cost beyond whatever AI you're already using.

---

## Contributing

Found a way to make the protocol tighter, or adapted it for a specific subject (e.g. a language-learning variant, a music-practice variant)? Open a PR. Keep additions general-purpose — the goal is one system that works for *any* topic, not a pile of subject-specific forks.

